silm:instances_papers_11_base_commutative_diagram_chapters_26_circuit_imprint_tensor_sections_01_three_axes_unpacked_concrete_anchor_3#learycube_apex silm:hasLongDescription "The LearyCube_apex is the abstract Leary cube apex: the 2x2x2 = 8-corner tensor structure with three orthogonal binary axes. In the paper's apparatus it appears as the symbol 'LearyCube_apex', a concrete instance grounded in the Mittens domain story; it serves as the anchor whose semantics every diagram, formula, and prose reference back to." .
